The fix introduces RCU (Read-Copy-Update) protection by wrapping the list iteration with `rcu_read_lock()` and `rcu_read_unlock()`. This ensures that while the list is being read, any concurrent modifications (like deletions) are safely managed, preventing access to freed memory and thus eliminating the use-after-free issue. The use of `list_for_each_entry_rcu` allows safe iteration over the list in a concurrent environment.


